 "note": "The AI features have no tools. Compose and thread summary stream text through server oRPC routes. The OpenRouter key is server-only through t3-env, so there is no browser model call. Compose output enters the editor only after the user clicks Save, so ai_tool_unbounded and ai_no_human_review do not apply. AI routes have a per-user rate limit of 2 per minute and an Arcjet PII check. Prisma runs only on the server, so row level security does not apply. Client-side role hiding in team-card, team-list, organization-header and app-sidebar is backed by server role checks in the team routes and by better-auth for org actions. No mock data or seed files. The landing logo cloud lists the real build tools. GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET are read in lib/auth.ts lines 52-53 but are missing from lib/env.ts and .env.example. Vendored components/ui/*, .agents/skills/*, worker-configuration.d.ts, pnpm-lock.yaml and images were skipped. No file was blocked.",
